 divides the remaining space between Gojo and an approaching object again and again. The object slows as it crosses increasingly tiny intervals and never completes the final distance under normal conditions.",
            "It is not simply an invisible wall. Gojo can automatically classify threats and allow harmless things such as light, air, or chosen people to pass while stopping dangerous objects."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Blue, Red, and Purple",
          bullets: [
            "Blue is the strengthened lapse of Limitless. It creates an impossible spatial deficit that produces powerful attraction and can also support high-speed movement.",
            "Red is the Cursed Technique Reversal. Positive energy reverses the technique's effect and produces violent repulsion.",
            "Hollow Purple combines the opposing spatial effects of Blue and Red into a devastating attack that tears through its path."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Teleportation and movement",
          paragraphs: [
            "Limitless can compress space to move Gojo or other people over distance, but the series repeatedly notes that teleportation operates under certain conditions. It should not be treated as unrestricted omnipresence.",
            "Blue can also manipulate Gojo's movement at close range, contributing to his acceleration, positioning, and striking power."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Ways to bypass Infinity",
          bullets: [
            "A Domain Expansion's sure-hit can reach through ordinary technique defenses while the domain is functioning.",
            "Domain Amplification can neutralize a technique on contact, although the user generally cannot operate their innate technique at the same time.",
            "Specialized cursed tools such as the Inverted Spear of Heaven can nullify cursed techniques.",
            "Later manga events demonstrate additional highly specific solutions that depend on adaptation and technique interpretation."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Common misconceptions",
          bullets: [
            "Infinity does not stop time.",
            "Hollow Purple is enormously destructive, but the manga does not simply define it as automatic existence erasure.",
            "The Six Eyes are not another part of Limitless; they are a separate ocular trait that allows Limitless to be mastered efficiently.",
            "Teleportation is an application with conditions, not proof that Gojo can appear anywhere without restriction."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "six-eyes": {
      verified: true,
      source: "Six_Eyes",
      sections: [
        {
          title: "What the Six Eyes provide",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Six Eyes give extraordinarily detailed perception of cursed energy. Their user can read energy flow, analyze techniques, and control cursed energy with microscopic precision.",
            "That precision reduces the cursed-energy loss involved in activating a technique to an extremely small amount. This is why Gojo can maintain demanding applications of Limitless for long periods without emptying his reserves through ordinary use."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Relationship with Limitless",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Six Eyes and Limitless are separate inherited traits. Limitless can appear within the Gojo clan without the Six Eyes, but mastering its full potential is considered practically impossible without the perception and efficiency the eyes provide.",
            "Gojo is overwhelming because he possesses both at once, not because either name is simply another word for the other."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Perception is not omniscience",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Six Eyes can reveal extraordinary cursed-energy information, but they do not automatically explain every hidden condition, intention, binding vow, or future development. A user still has to interpret what they perceive.",
            "They also do not guarantee that Gojo can react to every attack under every circumstance. Perception, interpretation, physical response time, surprise, and the mechanics of the opposing technique remain separate factors."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Why Gojo covers his eyes",
          paragraphs: [
            "The constant amount of visual and cursed-energy information is mentally tiring. A blindfold or dark glasses reduce the ordinary sensory load while still allowing Gojo to perceive far more than a normal sorcerer.",
            "Removing the covering gives him unobstructed vision when he needs maximum detail and control."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Common misconceptions",
          bullets: [
            "The Six Eyes are not an innate cursed technique.",
            "They do not provide literal knowledge of everything.",
            "Near-perfect efficiency does not mean Gojo has infinite cursed-energy reserves.",
            "Seeing cursed energy does not automatically reveal every conceptual property of a technique before it is used."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "ten-shadows": {
      verified: true,
      source: "Ten_Shadows_Technique",
      sections: [
        {
          title: "How the shikigami system works",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Ten Shadows Technique uses shadows as a medium to summon ten types of shikigami. The user begins with Divine Dogs and must defeat most other shikigami in an exorcism ritual before commanding them.",
            "A ritual can include outside participants, but victory with outside help does not grant control of the shikigami. This prevents a user from simply bringing a stronger sorcerer to tame every summon for them."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Shadows are more than portals",
          bullets: [
            "The user can hide within shadows and move through them.",
            "Objects and cursed tools can be stored inside the shadow, although the user bears their weight.",
            "Shadows can be shaped into pathways, ambush points, and unstable ground.",
            "A skilled user can partially manifest a shikigami instead of always summoning the complete body."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Destruction and Totality",
          paragraphs: [
            "When certain shikigami are completely destroyed, they cannot simply be summoned again. Their power may be inherited by another compatible shikigami through Totality.",
            "The inheritance system has compatibility rules; it is not established that every destroyed summon can transfer every trait to any surviving summon."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Mahoraga",
          paragraphs: [
            "Eight-Handled Sword Divergent Sila Divine General Mahoraga is the technique's most dangerous shikigami. No